Original commit body from 1c16999e9f62dbf5356a93fd41fc0842c87fd3f0:

Addresses WI-sulas. _extract_call_target named the chain's first
identifier as the receiver, so the emit site typed `v` for a call on
`v.p`. This put the head's external type in the module slot
(ch.pipeline.addHandler -> swift:Channel), and let the head's in-repo type
drive resolution (app.server.start() -> Application.start).

A value chain of 2+ hops on a lowercase, non-self head now contributes no
hint. The receiver expression is typed by WI-higob's walker or left
untyped. Unchanged: single hops, self heads (WI-sizas) and type heads
(URLSession.shared...).

Removing the wrong hint exposed those sites to method-call recovery,
whose premise ("a class the caller instantiates is the receiver") the
wrong hint had been refuting by accident. On hummingbird it guessed
router.middlewares.add(..) into Router.add 46 times, and every sampled one
was wrong. Swift now stamps meta.receiver = "field_chain" on such calls, a
value already in the receiver vocabulary for this shape (go uses it). The
recovery linker gains step 3y, refusing a field_chain receiver.

